1 NOTE CITATION
2 CONT
2 CONT AWARD OF BRONZE STAR MEDAL
2 CONT
2 CONT Private William H. Powell, Junior, 34 897 990, 517th Parachute Infantry
2 CONC , United States Army, for heroic achievement in action near Grand Haleu
2 CONC x, Belgium, 10 and 11 January 1945. After repulsing two attacks, Privat
2 CONC e Powell and his squad, although outnumbered, were subjected to a third a
2 CONC ssault by enemy mortars and artillery. By skillful timing and cordinate
2 CONC d fire they drove back repeated enemy attempts to overun their position
2 CONC . During this action one of the squad was killed and two were wounded. D
2 CONC espite this, and the concentrated enemy barrage, Private Powell and his w
2 CONC eakened squad knocked out five enemy guns and their crews. Over thirth-
2 CONC two enemy dead and many wounded were accounted for by their accurate fi
2 CONC re. Private Powell's heroic and determined devotion to duty was a decid
2 CONC ing factor in preventing an enemy breakthrough, and reflected great cre
2 CONC dit on himself and the military service. Entered the military service f
2 CONC rom Oxford, North Carolina.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT (Signed by)
2 CONT E. G. Chapman
2 CONT Major General, U. S. Army
2 CONT Commanding
