1 NOTE Obituary in News and Observer, Sept. 27, 1959
2 CONT MRS. KATHARINE K. POWELL
2 CONT OXFORD-Mrs Katharine Klingman Powell, widow of W. H. Powell, died sudde
2 CONC nly Sunday afternoon at her home of a heart condition.
2 CONT She was a member of St. Stephens Episcopal Church, the Woman's Auxiliar
2 CONC y, and the Intermediate Woman's Club. She was an alumna of St. Mary's S
2 CONC chool
2 CONT Surviving are three sons, W. H. Powell, Jr. of Spartanburg, S. C., Edwi
2 CONC n K. Powell of Atlanta, Ga. and Michael Powell with the U. S. Navy at P
2 CONC ortsmouth, Va.; two daughters; Mrs. Russell Clark and Mrs. Ben Williams
2 CONC , both of Raleigh; her mother, Mrs. O. C. Klingman and a brother, R. H. K
2 CONC lingman, both of Carmichael, Calif.: also seven grandchildren.
2 CONT Funeral plans will be announced
